    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1082">

                <pb facs="0794" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3902.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-28T10:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My April 27. Referring Brazilian Minister’s message, I have again addressed him
                    most urgently that in spite of Foreign Minister’s assurances we are positively
                    informed Americans detained at Cordoba, Aguascalientes and other places and have
                    requested Brazilian Minister again see Foreign Minister reiterating
                    representations in strongest manner, insisting that all Americans be allowed go
                    place of safety under safe conduct. Have also asked Brazilian Legation keep us
                    constantly informed.</p>
                <p>We are using all means at our disposal secure information that is reliable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
